title The name a missing build hid -- four witnesses take their own build, and the fourth names a roster that rotated six days ago
prompt The SILENCE seat prompt: roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, rota row N mod 5 advancing by hand past a repeat, QA on touch, read scope, ListAgents before a file moves; pick up the running thread and take the next infrastructure lap.
think ListAgents named one peer, grain-65, interactive, four hours old. Same macOS checkout, which is REDS %291 standing rather than a surprise. Named before any file moved.
think Rota N=3732 by git rev-list --count HEAD, row 2 -- FIRE, and fire was deep-read at 06:17 and again at 10:42 today. Air went at 05:43, water at 09:42, earth at 12:47. Row 0, AETHER -- Jupiter, why the work exists, the row that HEARS -- was the only one unread on this day's shelf, so I advanced by hand and said so. Its threshold, Follow Our Compass, the Lindy effect, and the Grain and the Crossing. The peer's 14:01 lap read the same row from the other bench; two hands heard the same three documents this hour, which is a fact about the fleet rather than a collision.
think Aether chose the lap before I had picked one. Its dual seat, the Grain and the Crossing, seats the strand in as many words: A GUARD THAT CANNOT RED GUARDS NOTHING -- a witness must be proven able to make a sound before its silence means anything. Its fixed seat, Lindy, says the same thing pointed at time: a checked claim stays audible, an asserted one fades. REDS %334 is exactly that sentence with a number on it.
think Reds first, and %334 was the one open row fully agent-closable. %291 is Keaton's word, %301 is five booked folds each its own lap, %306 and %326 and %328 are seats, %311 is Sound's language custody, %327 is Keaton's hand, %330 is its own design lap. %334 was OPEN on four remaining unbuilt pairs, and the prior lap had already read the fact that made this bench the right one: all four artifacts are ABSENT here.
think Reproduced before repairing. All four witnesses died with `rishi: line NN: CommandFailed` naming no cause -- the exact refusal the row calls a guard that guards nothing. This Mac is the clone the meter was written about, so the RED leg cost nothing to stage.
think The repair is six lines per witness in the shape comlink_topology_witness.rish seated: read the vendored toolchain into `zig`, `mkdir -p` the bin room, build, and assert the build BEFORE the invocation. The mkdir is not decoration -- the scan's own comment records that `rye build` refuses an absent -femit-bin directory, and a build line lacking it once passed the meter and would have failed on a clone.
think Rewrote each file through its original inode -- awk to a tmp, then `cat tmp > file` -- per the exec-bit law. Verified after: the two .sh fixtures still read 100755 in the index and -rwxr-xr-x in the tree, the five .rish and .rye still 100644. A mode moves no lines, so nothing else would have said so.
think Two comments were left describing the wrong statement by the insert -- the module-selftest lines in kumara and nakshatra now sat above a build block. Moved each back down to its own `let st`. A comment that describes the statement below it is load-bearing prose, and an insert that silently reassigns it is the same class of quiet drift this lap went on to book.
obs THE FOURTH WITNESS BUILT, THEN REFUSED -- AND THAT IS THE REPAIR WORKING. classical-vedic-astrology/seat_nakshatra died with error.ExampleWrong naming seat_nakshatra.zig:64 instead of a bare CommandFailed. A real defect the missing build had been standing in front of: the 20260823.201533 correction rotated the nakshatra roster by two into the Taittiriya order (Krittika at seat zero rather than Ashvini) and bumped the module's version string to that stamp, and THREE assertions kept the elder names -- the module's example expecting Shatabhishak at point 267, and the witness expecting "point 0 wears Ashvini" and "nakshatra Shatabhishak".
obs MEASURED RATHER THAN REASONED, before a byte was edited: `seat_nakshatra 267` prints `point 267 - seat 23 - nakshatra Uttara Bhadrapada`. The GEOMETRY never moved -- outfit_seat(267) reads 23 on both sides of the rotation -- so `seat 23` was the one assertion of four that stayed true, and the names are what rotated. Shatabhishak sits at 21 now; the module's own comment read `-- seat 23` beside the elder count's name, which is the arithmetic that gave the rotation away.
obs THE PAIRING IS THE LESSON AND IT IS SHARPER THAN %334'S OWN. witness_own_build_witness.rish records that all four remaining artifacts are PRESENT on the pier. A binary built before 20260823.201533 carries the elder roster and passes. So the same file could read GREEN there and die here, and neither reading was ever about the mapping it claimed to prove. A missing build does not merely make a witness useless on a clone -- it hides the defect the witness exists to catch, on every machine where a stale artifact still answers. That is %311 at one remove: there the harness supplied the needle, here the filesystem supplied a stale answer, and both pass because the checker never reached the checked.
obs Booked as REDS %343 (20260829.141956) on its own shelf, CLOSED on the drift, with the seat it leaves named rather than closed by arithmetic: seat_nakshatra_witness.rish is on no roster and named by no runner -- `grep -rl` finds one dated log, one method page, and the file itself -- so the next rotation of a silo roster has no clock either. Whether a witness in a room the manifest marks `personal` belongs on the standing roster is %328's open question wearing a different room.
obs THE CEILING BECAME A WALL. CEILING 4 -> 0, self_built 54 -> 58, absent_now 4 -> 0, verdict=ok. All four proven from DELETED artifacts rather than from a bench that had been building for weeks. The control's two ratchet plants move to 0 and 1 -- and one case beside them had to be repaired to survive the move: absent_never_gates asserted a literal `verdict=ok`, which at a wall of zero conflates the wall with the one-machine presence fact the case exists to isolate. It compares the two readings now and proves that changing PRESENCE ALONE moves nothing, which is what the case always meant and is ceiling-independent besides.
obs THE PIN WAS DEADLOCKED AND CLOSING %334 IS WHAT RELIEVED IT. reds_pin_capacity read pin_bytes=24571, headroom=5, 9 rows, 9 OPEN, 0 foldable, pin_deadlocked=1 -- a new red had nowhere to go, and the cure is Keaton's seat with three doors costed in 20260829-031804. I crossed none of them. %334 CAN close, so I closed it, and a closed row is foldable: the pin reads 23,765 with 811B free and 8 rows. %343 is still born on its own shelf, as %335 through %342 were, because the deadlock as a STRUCTURE is unchanged -- pin_deadlocked still reads 1, since no median row fits 811B.
obs ONE EDIT TO A STANDING ROW, AND ITS RULE READ FIRST. reds_fold.sh refuses any row carrying the bare uppercase word OPEN, which is looser than the status scan's last-bold-marker test; the two differ by four rows on purpose. So %334's `**OPEN** on the 46.` became `Stood open on the 46.` -- the historical claim kept in plain words, the bold marker spent on the new **CLOSED**. Checked rather than assumed: no folded row anywhere in the archive carries OPEN in its row line, so this is the convention every folded row already followed rather than a policy I invented.
obs THE COLD ROSTER ANSWERED NOTHING AND SAID SO. 92 guards, 84 green, 8 red, tree_moved=yes -- the peer landed two commits inside my 32-minute run, the third such collision in two laps. Of the 8: rule_twin is gate %7; width_check reads 331/329 files and 1265/1263 lines, exactly two each, and both are the peer's brushstroke/spread.rye and pond/apps/spread.rye at two authored usize apiece -- my touched .rye carries zero, checked by grep rather than by inference; remember_git_nib and nib_honesty are the shared-checkout nib artifact; three Pond rows are Hush's; and geode_libraries re-ran GREEN singly, a mid-move reading exactly as the prior lap found. None mine.
obs QA on touch: eight files graded before the first edit -- four witnesses at meter/service 75, the scan, control, witness and REDS at meter/service 90. Composite 94 (A) and 98 (A+), truth 100 across all eight. No frame pushed.
