recommend check-in (Keaton) -- A REPAIR'S FIRST RUN FOUND WHAT THE MISSING BUILD WAS HIDING. %334 closes at zero and its ratchet is a wall; %343 books the roster that rotated six days ago behind a witness that could not run. TWO GATES WANT YOUR WORD, both already on the card and neither crossed here: REDS %291, two Claude sessions on one macOS checkout, which spent a 32-minute roster on tree_moved for the third time in two laps; and the pin deadlock, whose three doors stand costed in 20260829-031804 -- closing %334 returned 811B of headroom without deciding any of them, and pin_deadlocked still reads 1. ONE SEAT IS NEW: whether a witness in a room the manifest marks `personal` belongs on the standing roster, which is %328's question in a different room.
